Certainly! To implement the save and cancel functionality for the menu editing form, we'll need to make a few changes to both the HTML template and the JavaScript file. Here's how we can achieve this:

1. In the HTML template (menus.html), add a cancel button next to the save button:

```html
<button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Salva</button>
<button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="cancelButton">Annulla</button>
```

2. In the JavaScript file (menu_management.js), add the following code to handle form submission and cancel button:

```javascript
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
    // ... existing code ...

    const form = document.querySelector('form');
    const cancelButton = document.getElementById('cancelButton');

    form.addEventListener('submit', function(e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        const formData = new FormData(form);

        fetch('/settings/update_menu', {
            method: 'POST',
            body: formData
        })
        .then(response => response.json())
        .then(data => {
            if (data.success) {
                alert('Menu aggiornato con successo!');
                location.reload(); // Reload the page to reflect changes
            } else {
                alert('Errore durante l\'aggiornamento del menu.');
            }
        });
    });

    cancelButton.addEventListener('click', function() {
        form.reset();
    });
});
```

3. In your Flask route (in the appropriate Python file), handle the form submission:

```python
@settings.route('/update_menu', methods=['POST'])
def update_menu():
    # Extract form data
    menu_id = request.form.get('id')
    name = request.form.get('name')
    # ... other fields ...

    # Update the menu in the database
    menu = Menu.query.get(menu_id)
    if menu:
        menu.name = name
        # ... update other fields ...
        db.session.commit()
        return jsonify({'success': True})
    else:
        return jsonify({'success': False})
```

These changes will allow you to save the modified menu data to the database and regenerate the menus. The cancel button will clear the form fields without making any changes. The page will reload after a successful save to reflect the updated menu structure.

